note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
note cqcase.om: scenario conductor, independent verifier and hidden-test judge for the DRA-184
note coding harness. It runs cqa (the agent), cqfix (SYNTHETIC scripted fixture) and the judges as
note separate processes (fork/execprog), cancels, kills (SIGKILL) and restarts cqa, and checks:
note   verifier  (no cqa code): every journal line well-formed; exactly one T; per step at most one
note             R, E and D, and a D for every E; no E after an X; the last D for each written path
note             matches the file on disk (length, FNV-1a 64); `git status` of the isolated worktree
note             shows changes to owned files only (own.txt), nothing else.
note   judge     the scenario's hidden test (tests/coding_qual/judges/judge-sN.py, never visible to
note             the agent) run in bwrap --unshare-all on the final worktree; PASS needs exit 0 and a
note             fresh random nonce line in its output.
note Usage:
note   cqcase synthetic BIN WORK BASE JUDGES        cases c1..c12 against cqfix (label SYNTHETIC)
note   cqcase real BIN WORK BASE JUDGES PORT        cases r1..r4 against a model on 127.0.0.1:PORT
note BASE is the fixture git repository with branches cq-s1 (scenario S1) and cq-s2 (S2, one
note planted regression); every case gets its own `git worktree add --detach` under WORK/<case>.
note Prints `CASE <name> PASS|FAIL step <k>` per case, `OBSERVED <name> state=.. judge=..` in real
note mode, then `CQCASE <LABEL> PASS cases=N` (exit 0) or `... FAIL failed=K cases=N` (exit 1).

text tsyn "synthetic"
text trl "real"
text tsynl "SYNTHETIC"
text treall "REAL"
text tcase "CASE "
text tpass " PASS\n"
text tfail " FAIL step "
text tobs "OBSERVED "
text tost " state="
text toj " judge="
text tojp "PASS"
text tojf "FAIL"
text tosd " writes="
text tosr " answers="
text tsum1 "CQCASE "
text tsum2 " PASS cases="
text tsum3 " FAIL failed="
text tsum4 " cases="
text tusage "cqcase: usage: cqcase synthetic BIN WORK BASE JUDGES | cqcase real BIN WORK BASE JUDGES PORT\n"
text tsl "/"
text tcqa "cqa"
text tfixb "cqfix"
text ttask "task"
text tcanc "cancel"
text tst8 "steps=8"
text tst6 "steps=6"
text tst3 "steps=3"
