text tcrW "crash=W"
text tjrn "/journal.log"
text tiss "/issue.txt"
text town "/own.txt"
text ttst "/test.txt"
text trepo "/repo"
text trepos "/repo/"
text tscr ".script"
text tfixo ".fix"
text tout1 ".out1"
text tout2 ".out2"
text tout3 ".out3"
text tjudo ".judge"
text tgito ".git"
text twto ".wt"
text t64 "64"
text tport "PORT "
text tgit "/usr/bin/git"
text tgc "-C"
text twt "worktree"
text tadd "add"
text tqq "-q"
text tdet "--detach"
text tbr1 "cq-s1"
text tbr2 "cq-s2"
text tstat "status"
text tpor "--porcelain"
text tuall "-uall"
text tbw "/usr/bin/bwrap"
text tpy "/usr/bin/python3"
text tbwa "--unshare-all\n--die-with-parent\n--ro-bind\n/\n/\n--dev\n/dev\n--proc\n/proc\n--tmpfs\n/tmp\n--ro-bind\n"
text tbwb "--chdir\n"
text tbwc "--\n/usr/bin/python3\n-B\n-m\nunittest\ndiscover\n-s\ntests\n-q\n"
text tjs1 "judge-s1.py"
text tjs2 "judge-s2.py"
text tbB "-B"
text tnl "\n"
text tsp " "
text is1 "Rename the helper require_text in textkit/norm.py to ensure_text and update every caller (textkit/words.py). Behaviour and error messages must not change.\n"
text is2 "The test suite fails: tests/test_words.py test_truncate_words. Find the bug in the code and fix it. Do not change the tests.\n"
text ow1 "textkit/norm.py\ntextkit/words.py\n"
text ow2 "textkit/words.py\n"
text bnorm1 "def ensure_text(name, value):\n    \"\"\"Raise TypeError naming the parameter when value is not a str; return value.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        raise TypeError(f\"{name} must be a str, got {type(value).__name__}\")\n    return value\n"
text bword1 "from .norm import ensure_text\n\n\ndef count_words(s):\n    \"\"\"Number of whitespace-separated words in s.\"\"\"\n    ensure_text(\"s\", s)\n    return len(s.split())\n\n\ndef title_case(s):\n    \"\"\"Every word with its first letter upper-cased and the rest lower-cased, single spaces.\"\"\"\n    ensure_text(\"s\", s)\n    return \" \".join(w[:1].upper() + w[1:].lower() for w in s.split())\n\n\ndef truncate_words(s, n):\n    \"\"\"The first n words of s joined by single spaces; all of them when s has n words or fewer.\"\"\"\n    ensure_text(\"s\", s)\n    words = s.split()\n    return \" \".join(words[:n]) if len(words) > n else \" \".join(words)\n"
text bword2 "from .norm import require_text\n\n\ndef count_words(s):\n    \"\"\"Number of whitespace-separated words in s.\"\"\"\n    require_text(\"s\", s)\n    return len(s.split())\n\n\ndef title_case(s):\n    \"\"\"Every word with its first letter upper-cased and the rest lower-cased, single spaces.\"\"\"\n    require_text(\"s\", s)\n    return \" \".join(w[:1].upper() + w[1:].lower() for w in s.split())\n\n\ndef truncate_words(s, n):\n    \"\"\"The first n words of s joined by single spaces; all of them when s has n words or fewer.\"\"\"\n    require_text(\"s\", s)\n    words = s.split()\n    return \" \".join(words[:n]) if len(words) > n else \" \".join(words)\n"
text bjunk "import unittest\n"
text tpyo "```python\n"
text tfence "```\n"
note Scripts: records separated by ~, each MS^CONTENT (MS = delay in ms, X = a context error);
note @1 @2 @3 @4 in CONTENT expand to a python block holding bnorm1 / bword1 / bword2 / bjunk.
text sc1 "0^LIST\n~0^READ textkit/norm.py\n~0^WRITE textkit/norm.py\n@1~0^WRITE textkit/words.py\n@2~0^TEST\n~0^DONE\n"
text sc2 "0^TEST\n~0^READ textkit/words.py\n~0^WRITE textkit/words.py\n@3~0^TEST\n~0^DONE\n"
text sc3 "0^READ textkit/words.py\n~3000^WRITE textkit/words.py\n@3~0^DONE\n"
text sc4 "0^LIST\n~0^WRITE textkit/norm.py\n@1~4000^WRITE textkit/words.py\n@2~0^WRITE textkit/words.py\n@2~0^TEST\n~0^DONE\n"
text sc7 "0^WRITE tests/test_words.py\n@4~0^DONE\n"
text sc8 "X^-"
text sc9 "0^I am not sure what to do here.\n"
text sc10 "0^READ ../../../../etc/passwd\n~0^READ /etc/passwd\n~0^WRITE ../escape.py\n@1~0^READ .git/config\n~0^DONE\n"
text n1 "c1 cross-file-change"
text n2 "c2 failing-test-fixed"
text n3 "c3 cancel-mid-task"
text n4 "c4 resume-after-sigkill"
